Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/18

## Summary

There were no random events. This adds the Genie random event in a new module `content/events/random-events`, scheduled by the OSRS Wiki's random event spawn mechanics ("Random events", section "Spawn mechanics", which quotes Mod Ash for each rule). Content area from #353. This push replaces the first version with a rewrite checked against the wiki, on current `main` (`829b9477d`).

- **When.** The next event is due 1-2 hours after the last one, on a real-time clock that keeps running while the player is logged out. The due time is stored in a persistent player attribute (`random_event_next_at`, epoch milliseconds), so it survives logout and restarts. A soft timer checks every 5 minutes of play (500 ticks) whether it is due.
- **Offline.** If the event came due while the player was offline, the due time moves forward by 10-70 minutes on login, as many times as needed to land in the future, and keeps counting.
- **Where not.** When it is due and the player is somewhere random events are not allowed, the event is missed and a new 1-2 hours is rolled. The places covered: inside a bank with a bank booth (a booth within 7 tiles) or in front of a bank chest (within 2 tiles), except Ferox Enclave; the Grand Exchange's stone square; the God Wars Dungeon, Ancient Cavern, Waterbirth Island Dungeon, Ruins of Tapoyauik and Charred Dungeon (cache areas); and instances (boss lairs and minigames run in instances here).
- **Transformed.** No event while the player's model is altered (transformation ring, greegree): it is missed in the same way. A Genie that is already out leaves at once if the player transforms (Mod Ash: "the genie would delete itself when it realised you'd equipped that").
- **Busy.** An open interface or a Make-X repeat (a pending weak queue, which is how Make-X loops run here) holds a due event back. It is retried every tick and spawns as soon as the player is free.
- **One at a time.** No second event NPC while the Genie is out.
- **The Genie** (timings, anims, sounds and messages from RSProx recordings of the official game, see the notes): appears beside the player in a puff of smoke (spotanim `smokepuff`, sounds 2301 and `smokepuff`), faces them, waves and says "Greetings, Master/Mistress <name>!". Every 10 ticks he follows them, banks included (wiki, 1 November 2023), waves and calls them by name with one of the three transcript lines. Talk-to gives the lamp with the game message "Your reward is: 1 x Lamp." and the transcript's line; he leaves 10 ticks after Talk-to whatever the dialogue is doing, so an interrupted Talk-to never loses the lamp or leaves him behind. Talked to again before he goes, he says "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress." (Transcript:Genie, completed event). Dismiss sends him away. Ignored, he says "Maybe later." in place of his tenth call (a minute after he appears) and leaves 3 ticks later. He always leaves in a puff of smoke. Another player's Talk-to gets "Sorry, I'm trying to talk to someone else, but he/she seems to be ignoring me." (the owner's pronoun).
- **The lamp:** Rub opens the stat chooser ("Choose the stat you wish to be advanced!") and gives 10 x the chosen skill's level in XP, multiplied by the world's XP rate like other XP (`statAdvance`, as upstream's quest lamp does), then shows "Your wish has been granted!<br>You have been awarded <xp> <Skill> XP!" with sound `found_gem`. With a full inventory it is dropped at the player's feet for 3 hours (wiki trivia, Mod Ash: rewards are dropped and stay up to three hours).
- `::randomevent` summons him (like `::star`), bypassing the schedule.

The zones where events are missed or allowed (the listed dungeon areas, Ferox Enclave, the Grand Exchange square) are rows of a server-only `dbtable.random_event_zones` in a new `random-events` pack (an area, or a centre and radius, per row, and whether events are allowed), like upstream's other server-only dbtables.

New server-only gamevals: synth `macro_genie_appear` = 2301 (the arrival sound has no name in the cache); timers `random_event` (the 5-minute check) and `random_event_genie` (the Genie's calls), written as `-1` and assigned by `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py` (65534 and 65533, one below the cannon PR's timer so the two don't clash); `dbtable.random_event_zones` and its seven `dbrow.random_event_zone_*` rows, assigned the same way.

