## How it was tested

Unit/integration: `GenieRandomEventTest` (9, integration), on the schedule and the lamp hand-over (AGENTS.md):
- the due time is 1-2 h ahead, persisted, and a relog does not restart it;
- an event due while offline moves 10-70 min forward;
- a due event spawns him and rolls the next one;
- in a bank (booth 2 tiles away) it is missed and re-rolled;
- transformed: missed, and a Genie already out leaves;
- an open interface delays it until closed;
- a Make-X weak queue delays it;
- an interrupted hand-over still gives exactly one lamp, and the Genie leaves;
- an ignored Genie stays 3 ticks after "Maybe later.", gives no lamp then, and leaves.

On this branch: CI (`assemble test integration`, boot to ready) and Formatting pass on our fork; the random-events module's `integration` passes (`GenieRandomEventTest` 9/9). `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts.

In game (desktop RuneLite on a branch server, fresh account), on 068aabee2, before the zones moved into the dbtable and before the changes from the recordings (call every 10 ticks, wave, smoke and sounds, the reward message, the Rub message box, leaving 10 ticks after Talk-to and 3 ticks after "Maybe later."). These still need an in-game run on this commit; our QA gate does it before the PR is marked ready:
- `::randomevent`: the Genie appears beside the player, follows when they walk away, and is gone a minute later when ignored.
- Talk-to: the lamp arrives as the line opens; the Genie leaves also when the dialogue is left open or another one replaces it; exactly one lamp each time.
- A second Talk-to before he goes: "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress.".
- `::randomevent` with a Genie out: "Your Genie is already here."; Dismiss removes him.
- Full inventory: exactly one lamp on the floor under the player.
- Rub: 10 x the skill level x the world's XP rate.
- Scheduling: too slow to wait for in game (1-2 h); the tests cover it.

